cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software (below) and the associated paper."
title: "Fractal Analysis of Seismicity and Fault Network Geometry: R and Python Workflows (Marmara / NAFZ)"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible R and Python workflow for quantifying the scale invariance of an
  earthquake catalogue: box-counting dimension (D0) and correlation dimension (D2)
  of the epicentre distribution, box-counting dimension of the fault-trace network,
  and the maximum-likelihood Gutenberg-Richter b-value, with magnitude-of-completeness
  selection and Gardner-Knopoff declustering. Demonstrated on the Marmara region of
  the North Anatolian Fault Zone.
